            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "\\begin{align*}D-S&=999p+99q+9r\\\\D-S&=9(111p+11q+r)\\end{align*}",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p24-q37-answer-conclusion",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "right",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Both D and D − S are multiples of 9, so S is a multiple of 9. If the number equals its reverse, the difference and digit sum are both 0.",
